    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d203">

                <pb facs="0247" n="235" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg235"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51/8–1845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacVeagh</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-25T14:00:00-04:00">August 25, 1945—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>869. Your 866 and 867.<anchor n="61" xml:id="d203-f1"/> While the Export-Import
                    Bank may make moderate loans to aid in the reconstruction of Greece there is no
                    basis for astronomical expectations. The figure named by Varvaressos, 250
                    million dollars, represents official request presented to the Export-Import Bank
                    Aug 20; but Greek Embassy has been informed by the Bank that question must be
                    presented to full Bank Board and no indication can be given as to when Board
                    will act or what amount if any may be approved.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d203-f1" n="61" xml:id="d203-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed; for summary, see footnote 60, <ref target="#pg234">p.
